        ["sun-tzu","Sun Tzu","c. 6th century BCE–?","Traditionally associated with the state of Qi or Wu; uncertain","Unknown; historical details uncertain","Strategist; traditionally described as a general","Traditionally associated with the state of Wu","Sun Tzu is traditionally credited with The Art of War, but his identity, dates, and biography remain disputed.","The text attributed to him discusses strategy, intelligence, planning, and the use of force.","His influence on military thought is extensive, though authorship and historicity are not settled.","china-comanders/sun-tzu.jpg","https://www.britannica.com/biography/Sunzi"],
        ["chiang-kai-shek","Chiang Kai-shek","1887–1975","Fenghua, Zhejiang, China","Taipei, Taiwan","Generalissimo; political and military leader","National Revolutionary Army; Republic of China","Chiang trained in Japan and rose within the Nationalist movement after the 1911 Revolution.","He led Nationalist forces during the Second Sino-Japanese War and the Chinese Civil War, later governing from Taiwan.","A major twentieth-century Chinese leader whose legacy includes both wartime resistance and authoritarian rule.","china-comanders/chang-kai.jpg","https://www.britannica.com/biography/Chiang-Kai-shek"]
