        ["saddam-hussein","Saddam Hussein","1937–2006","Al-Awja, near Tikrit, Iraq","Baghdad, Iraq","President; commander in chief","Iraqi Armed Forces; Ba'athist Iraq","Saddam rose through the Ba'ath Party and consolidated power in Iraq during the 1970s.","As president, he led Iraq during the Iran-Iraq War and the 1990 invasion of Kuwait; he was captured in 2003 and executed in 2006.","His rule was marked by dictatorship, wars, repression, and mass atrocities; military history must include this context.","iraq-coamnders/saddam-husein.jpg","https://www.britannica.com/biography/Saddam-Hussein"]
