        ["mehmed-ii","Mehmed II","1432–1481","Edirne, Ottoman Empire","Hünkâr Çayırı, Ottoman Empire","Sultan; military commander","Ottoman Empire","Mehmed became sultan as a young ruler and pursued the conquest of Constantinople.","He captured Constantinople in 1453 and expanded Ottoman power across the Balkans and Anatolia.","His conquest transformed the Ottoman state and made Constantinople its imperial capital.","turkey-comanders/mehmedII.jpg","https://www.britannica.com/biography/Mehmed-II-Ottoman-sultan"],
        ["hayreddin-barbarossa","Hayreddin Barbarossa","c. 1478–1546","Lesbos, Ottoman Empire (birth year approximate)","Istanbul, Ottoman Empire","Grand admiral","Ottoman Navy","Barbarossa rose from privateering in the Mediterranean to become the Ottoman Empire's leading admiral.","He commanded Ottoman naval forces, including at the Battle of Preveza in 1538.","His leadership helped establish Ottoman naval power in the Mediterranean; birth year is approximate.","turkey-comanders/ayredin-barbarosa.jpg","https://www.britannica.com/biography/Barbarossa-Ottoman-admiral"],
        ["suleiman-the-magnificent","Suleiman the Magnificent","1494–1566","Trabzon, Ottoman Empire","Szigetvár, Kingdom of Hungary","Sultan; commander in chief","Ottoman Empire","Suleiman inherited a powerful empire and led military campaigns while also overseeing legal and administrative reforms.","His reign saw campaigns in Central Europe and the Mediterranean, including the siege of Vienna and the conquest of much of Hungary.","Known in Ottoman tradition as the Lawgiver, his reign marked the empire's political and cultural high point.","turkey-comanders/suleiman.jpg","https://www.britannica.com/biography/Suleyman-the-Magnificent"],
        ["mustafa-kemal-ataturk","Mustafa Kemal Atatürk","1881–1938","Salonika, Ottoman Empire","Istanbul, Turkey","Marshal; president","Ottoman Army; Turkish Armed Forces","Kemal was an Ottoman officer who became prominent at Gallipoli and led the Turkish national movement after the First World War.","He commanded nationalist forces in the Turkish War of Independence and founded the Republic of Turkey in 1923.","Founder and first president of modern Turkey; the exact birth date is not established.","turkey-comanders/mustafa-kemal.jpg","https://www.britannica.com/biography/Kemal-Ataturk"],
        ["enver-pasha","Enver Pasha","1881–1922","Istanbul, Ottoman Empire","Ab-i-Derya, present-day Tajikistan","Ottoman general; war minister","Ottoman Army","Enver was a Young Turk officer who rose to power after the 1908 revolution.","As war minister during the First World War, he was one of the Ottoman Empire's principal leaders and later fought in Central Asia.","His role in Ottoman wartime policy and the Armenian genocide is central to assessments of his legacy.","turkey-comanders/enver-pasha.jpg","https://www.britannica.com/biography/Enver-Pasa"]
